# personal strategy notes stay off the public repo
ge-flipping-guide.md
# one-shot local utility from an old cleanup task
cleanup.html
# local Claude Code settings stay private; skills are part of the repo
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# disposable probe-run artifacts (see PROBE.md)
tools/probe/out/
# transient tracker→analyst handoff, carried by the human per BRIEFING.md;
# its contents are quoted in the dated BRIEF, the raw export stays local
briefings/flags-pending.json
# ANALYSIS EXPORTS — the read-exports from the three pull surfaces
# (analysis-paper / -gates / -prospecting / -all, plus the browser's " (1)"
# duplicate-download suffix). These are the user's own trading record: the repo
# carries the tool and its documentation, never the data it produced. Matched
# in any directory, since a download lands wherever the browser puts it.
analysis-*.json
# the localStorage state backup from the Flip Log tab — same reasoning, and it
# is a full dump rather than a curated read
gef-backup*.json
# the Downloads collector's landing zone (tools/inbox/sweep.sh). Same reasoning
# as the analysis exports themselves: the repo carries the tool, never the data
# it produced. Ignored in full, whatever lands here.
# ANCHORED to the repo root: a bare `inbox/` matches a directory of that name at
# ANY depth, and it silently swallowed tools/inbox/sweep.sh — the collector
# itself — which would have shipped the rule without the thing it describes.
/inbox/
